      "description": "Watch NEC Nijmegen vs Telstar highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Eredivisie match on 2026-08-08 presented a classic footballing tale of dominance versus clinical efficiency. While one side controlled the tempo and the ball, the other seized their moments with surgical precision to define the outcome. Telstar’s Early Blitz The match ignited within seconds of the kickoff. In the very 1st minute, Abdelnor Soualhia delivered a pinpoint ball that found Patrick Brouwer , who executed a stunning right-footed volley to give Telstar an immediate lead. NEC Nijmegen scrambled to respond, earning several corners through Sami Ouaissa , but their set-piece deliveries failed to find a target in a crowded box. The visitors doubled their advantage in the 24th minute, capitalizing on another defensive lapse. Patrick Brouwer turned provider this time, setting up Rui Mendes , who made no mistake with a composed left-footed finish. Despite NEC Nijmegen holding the lion's share of possession, they went into the break trailing by two goals, struggling to convert their territorial dominance into clear-cut chances. Sierhuis Sparks a Comeback Attempt The second half saw a flurry of tactical changes as NEC Nijmegen pushed desperately for a way back into the game. The introduction of Kaj Sierhuis proved inspired. In the 83rd minute, a move involving Clement Bischoff allowed Dusan Tadic to slide a pass to Kaj Sierhuis , who buried his shot into the back of the net. The goal electrified the stadium and set up a grandstand finish. Desperate Final Charges As the clock ticked toward the 90th minute, NEC Nijmegen threw everything forward, maintaining 71% possession throughout the contest. Bryan Linssen saw a goal-bound header saved comfortably by Ronald Koeman , who was later cautioned for time-wasting as Telstar clung to their lead. Despite six minutes of added time and relentless pressure from Emre Mor and Clement Bischoff , the visitors held firm to secure a hard-fought victory in front of 12,650 fans."
